# Scope
Four supported languages: en/ko/ja/zh. Recent main-menu labels, Work and parallel controls, gateway controls, debug controls, SSE discovery and Work settings responses had hardcoded English/Korean text.

# Changes
- recent_menu_text provides four-language entries with UI_TEXT fallback; raw command identifiers and user instructions are not translated.
- provider_option_panel uses locale for recent labels and display states, preserving raw option_prompt_default values.
- work_parallel_menu accepts explicit language for rows and uses configured language for save/error messages.
- Work save responses and recent external-event discovery controls use locale; runtime entrypoint forwards configured language.
- Main recently added menu labels use the same four-language entries.

# Evidence
- Focused provider option, Work option, parallel menu, external event, prelaunch projection suites: 27 tests passed. Ruff and diff checks passed.
- Initial isolated four-language capture launched the actual app, but images showed only main menu; not accepted as options-panel verification.
- Second driver attempt failed exit3221225786; no claim of UI verification.
- Third isolated four-language run uses longer transition wait and is pending. Only owned conhost descendants are stopped; no live routers touched.

# Pending
Inspect actual options screenshots, close remaining localization gaps, commit/push, verify published package and installed behavior. Task is not complete.
